      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to be cautious with combining high levels of caffeine, especially with green tea extract. Combining 100-200mg of caffeine and ~50-100mg of green tea extract can be quite high, particularly with your coffee habit. Given your high caffeine tolerance, consider starting with a lower dose on your first few mornings to assess your body's response. A typical recommendation is about 100-150mg of caffeine (two cups of coffee) and around 50-100mg of green tea extract. Always monitor how you feel and consult a healthcare professional before making significant changes to your routine.",
